>> title: Biryani
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: chicken, rice, indian, saffron, layered
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: chicken biryani, biriyani, briyani, dum biryani, hyderabadi biryani, birani
>> pairs-with: birista, raita, mint-chutney
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the rice is boiled until it bends but still snaps, because a grain cooked through before the pot is layered steams to paste

>> step: marinate 2 hr
Marinate @bone-in chicken thighs{2 1/2%lb}(1.1 kg; skinned and slashed) with @thick yogurt{1%cup}(240 g), @ginger-garlic paste{2%Tbs}(34 g), @Kashmiri chile powder{1%Tbs}, @garam masala{2%tsp}, @mint{1/4%cup}(chopped), @cilantro{1/4%cup}(chopped) and @kosher salt{2%tsp} ~marinate{2%hr}.

>> step: boil 5 min, until it bends but still snaps
Boil @basmati rice{2 1/2%cup}(500 g; rinsed until the water runs clear, then soaked 30 minutes and drained) in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) with @green cardamom{4%pods}, @cloves{4}, @bay leaf{1} and @kosher salt{2%Tbs} ~boil{5%min}, until a grain bends between the fingers and still snaps in the middle, then drain it at once.

>> step: soak 10 min, until the milk goes orange
Soak @saffron{1%large pinch} in @warm milk{1/4%cup}(60 mL) ~soak{10%min}, until the milk has gone orange.

>> step: layer the pot, meat under rice
Layer @&(~3)marinated chicken{} in the bottom of a #heavy pot{}, the @&(~2)parboiled rice{} over it, then @&(~1)saffron milk{} spooned across in stripes with @birista{1%cup}(the fried-onion recipe) and @melted ghee{3%Tbs}(42 g).

>> step: seal the lid on and steam 35 min on the lowest heat
Seal @&(~1)layered pot{} — the lid clamped under a rope of @stiff flour dough{4%oz}(115 g; flour and water, no more) pressed round the rim — and ~steam{35%min} on the lowest heat, on a diffuser if you have one.

Dum is the whole thing: the pot is shut and the rice finishes in the steam from below. Break the seal at the table.
